# A deep recursion that enters a second recursion at every level runs out of
# stack inside whichever one is on top when the stack ends, and the engines
# end at different depths. When the report named the cycle last entered,
# native named `small` and the interpreter `big`. An overflow names no place
# (kanso#1987), so both print the sentence alone.
fn small 0
  0

fn small k
  1 + small (k - 1)

fn big n
  1 + big (n + small 3)

pub play = print (big 0)
